# Public documentation

Anything that ships in this repository (README, ADRs, CONTRIBUTING, code comments, PR text, release notes) is public.

## Do

- Describe TenseMem by its properties: deterministic resolver, enforced cardinality, freshness-aware reads, contamination guard, durable corrections.
- Prefer reproducible metrics and scenario descriptions over naming other products.
- Keep ADRs focused on *our* decision, alternatives in abstract terms ("LLM decides updates", "agent tool calls"), not brand names.

## Do not

- Name competitor products or projects in public docs or PR descriptions.
- Commit the private design doc (`TenseMem-Design-Doc.md` or similar) or any file that contains internal competitor analysis.
- Paste API tokens, PyPI tokens, or credentials into the repo.

## When design changes

- Significant decisions → new or updated ADR in `docs/adr/`.
- User-visible API or CLI changes → update README in the same PR.
- Internal-only notes stay in the local private design doc outside this repository.
